WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.330
Over the course of ten years, numerous storylines,
and countless changes, The Walking Dead probably

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.019
couldn't help but leave behind a bunch of
loose ends.

00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:11.730
Here's a look at some of the major burning
questions that the series has yet to answer.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:16.750
We last see a critically wounded Rick in season
9, injuring himself in a heroic attempt to

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.000
save his friends and loved ones from a massive
herd of Walkers.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.520
What the other survivors don't know is that
Rick just barely survives his act of self-sacrifice,

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.530
and is rescued by the mysterious Anne.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:30.571
Anne's allies gather the pair into a helicopter
to fly off to parts unknown, after which the

00:00:30.571 --> 00:00:34.370
show jumps forward years later — with no
sign of Rick in the interim as far as the

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.989
other protagonists are concerned.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:39.610
In season 10, Michonne discovers evidence
on a grounded military boat that Rick may

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:43.480
have survived the ordeal — among a host
of scavenged goods, she finds his boots and

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.719
cell phone, along with a log entry that suggests
he may be alive and is potentially in New

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:48.719
Jersey.

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:49.780
She sets off to find him.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.319
Now, we know a few things about the mysterious
group who took Rick — the helicopter he

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.690
left in belongs to the Civic Republic Military.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:59.870
That group is advanced, militaristic, and
a part of the Alliance of the Three, the group

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:04.049
of fortified partner cities which we've learned
more about in the Walking Dead's spinoffs.

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:07.539
So while we have a general idea of where Rick's
journey has taken him, the details of what

00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:11.340
his life has been like since his departure
are still very vague, and we have no idea

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.990
what the intervening years have done for Rick's
circumstances or his character.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:18.180
It seems we'll find out in the Rick-centric
movies that continue his story.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:23.200
In the years since Rick's disappearance and
murky season 9 fate, fan favorite Michonne

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:27.299
has become the leader of the Alexandria Safe
Zone as well as the adoptive mother of Judith

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:28.299
Grimes.

00:01:28.299 --> 00:01:32.189
We last see her in the episode "What We Become"
as she sets off north upon her discovery that

00:01:32.189 --> 00:01:35.840
Rick may be alive, determined to discover
the fate of the man she still loves.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.500
"What We Become" has been confirmed as being
the last appearance of the character on The

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.770
Walking Dead, so we are unlikely to discover
the answer to Michonne's fate within the show

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.899
as it wraps up its final story arcs.

00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:49.729
This is obviously an unhappy end for fans
of the series, as Michonne is a pivotal and

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:50.750
well-loved character.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.649
So... what will become of her?

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:55.780
Despite the character's absence from the rest
of the series, Michonne would be a natural

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.090
fit to return in the Rick-centric films, so
fans can probably expect a resolution to her

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.890
story whenever those start rolling out.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:06.460
Another mystery concerns the fate of Eugene's
group, who are last seen captured by a cadre

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:10.380
of mysterious armed soldiers at the end of
season 10, episode 16.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.830
The show hasn't revealed who these soldiers
are yet, but the scene is a note-perfect recreation

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:18.640
of a sequence in the comic books that marks
the debut of the massive community known as

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.740
the Commonwealth.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.300
In the comics, the Commonwealth are a large,
well-organized network of communities that

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.110
attempt to "restart civilization" following
the devastation of the zombie plague.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:30.441
It seems safe to assume that the attack is
our first introduction to the group, but the

00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:34.360
show has deviated from the books that inspire
it before — until The Walking Dead tells

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.450
us outright who these people are, there's
no way of knowing for sure.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.390
“Charleston, West Virginia.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.930
Southern railyards, about a mile south of
the Kanawha River.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:46.210
One week, can you be there?”

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:49.560
When Eugene sets out to meet the mysterious
Stephanie, he approaches his meeting from

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.950
a hopeful place.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:54.790
After a long history of unrequited feelings
for Rosita, Eugene is understandably happy

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.560
at the idea of a potential romance with this
mysterious woman he sets out to meet for the

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.620
first time.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:04.410
When he instead encounters an unexpected trap
at the intended meeting, he has to be suspicious.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.180
Is Stephanie intentionally setting Eugene
up for a trap?

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:11.200
Or is it a well-intentioned meetup that's
intercepted in ways she can't control?

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.340
From Eugene's perspective, there could be
any number of explanations.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.900
The comic books do show that Stephanie has
a connection to the Commonwealth, the group

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:22.230
whose white-armored soldiers trap and capture
Eugene and company, yet eventually she and

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:25.620
Eugene do start a relationship despite this
frightening experience.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.220
The show's take on this relationship could
go in an entirely different direction.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.000
Either way, Eugene's plans for romance have
hit at least a pretty major snag.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.151
Two major series events — Rick's season
9 departure and Eugene's season 10 capture

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:42.550
— set us up for two major new civilizations
in the world of The Walking Dead in the Commonwealth

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.120
and the Civic Republic.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.980
What does the existence of these groups mean
for the future of the show, and what is their

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.980
relationship to each other?

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.840
The Civic Republic is an advanced authoritarian
society and part of the Alliance of the Three,

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.180
an allied network of fortified cities including
Omaha, Nebraska; Portland, Oregon; and the

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:02.160
Civic Republic itself, which is geographically
around Pennsylvania.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.540
It boasts 200,000 citizens and stands as the
largest civilization in the show world to

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.540
date.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:11.260
The Commonwealth is an Ohio-based network
of communities with around 50,000 citizens

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.580
and its own well-organized standing army.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:17.820
It's a central civilization in the comics,
and as such there's much more available information

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:18.820
on it.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.880
It's a thoroughly hierarchical class system,
running in practice like a feudal monarchy

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.490
where people are locked into the jobs they
had before the apocalypse.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:29.500
While the two organizations are distinct and
should have strong roles in the future of

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.320
the show, we don't know what their relationships
to each other are.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.380
As two of the largest civilizations we've
seen so far, each with large, technologically

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.040
advanced militaries, they're all but certain
to at least know about each other.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.510
At the same time, the Commonwealth of the
comics isn't a member of the Alliance of the

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.820
Three, since the latter group isn't a part
of the comic book storyline.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.340
How are these two organizations connected,
if they are at all?

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.060
The future of the show and its world may lie
in the relationships between these societies

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.660
— we just don't know yet what they are yet.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:01.380
Late in season 10, we see the introduction
of a mysterious masked warrior alongside Maggie.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:05.510
Wielding dual curved blades, he's first seen
during a rescue of Gabriel, who's barricaded

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:08.780
in a hospital that's being besieged by a group
of Whisperers.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.720
The Whisperers barge in and easily overtake
Gabriel.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.720
It seems as though all is lost before the
masked warrior enters and effortlessly slaughters

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.190
the attacking Whisperers, the last of which
is taken out by Maggie.

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:23.180
The only clue we have to his identity is her
cryptic line of introduction, which isn't

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:25.240
very specific.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.790
"It's okay.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:34.120
He's with me."

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:38.830
We know a few things from this brief encounter:
the masked survivor is a he, a skilled warrior,

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.950
and Maggie clearly trusts him.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:44.330
Other than those sparse details, we have yet
to learn much of anything about who's under

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:48.760
the mask, what his relation to Maggie is,
or... anything else about him, really.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:51.840
Hopefully we'll be seeing a lot more of him
— and getting more answers — in future

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:52.840
episodes.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:57.390
Virgil, first introduced in season 10, is
still a very mysterious character.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:01.150
We first encounter him as a researcher in
the capture of Oceanside, one who promises

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.830
Michonne a weapon that will help against the
Whisperers.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:08.310
Virgil accompanies Michonne on the excursion
that marks her major discovery of Rick's apparent

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:11.040
survival, leading to her own subsequent departure
from the show.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.889
He betrays her, trapping and drugging her
and causing her to have a series of disturbing

00:06:14.889 --> 00:06:16.300
hallucinations.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:20.730
That betrayal serves as a prelude to the discovery
that Virgil has also been keeping his coworkers

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.770
captive for quite some time.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:27.170
She overpowers him, and when Michonne discovers
Rick may be alive, she lets Virgil live and

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:28.710
sets off on her journey.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:32.300
When Michonne leaves Virgil, she seems to
see some good in him despite his treachery

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.670
and a history of having done some bad things.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:35.919
Is he trustworthy?

00:06:35.919 --> 00:06:37.950
If not, Connie is certainly in jeopardy.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:40.690
Her fate, and the response of Daryl and others,
remains mysterious.

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:41.690
Negan's free.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.930
Our introduction to Negan comes when he's
the vicious leader of the Saviors, a group

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:50.110
who describe themselves as bringing civilization
and order back to the world — albeit at

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.720
a terribly steep cost.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:57.639
“Whatever you do, no matter what, you don’t
mess with the new world order.”

00:06:57.639 --> 00:07:02.300
Every community they encounter is subjected
to their rule, until a coalition of the Alexandria

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:06.590
Safe Zone, Hilltop Colony, the Kingdom, and
Oceanside break their power.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:11.080
Until that time, Negan demands absolute loyalty,
often killing a member of a rebellious group

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.080
to reinforce his rule and subjugate those
he conquers.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.180
Early on, in an effort to break the will of
Rick and his group, Negan brutally kills Abraham

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:21.330
and Glenn with his barbed-wire-wrapped baseball
bat, Lucille.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:24.510
This leaves Maggie, Glenn's wife, tragically
widowed.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.340
Following the defeat of Negan's Saviors, Maggie
is understandably angry at Rick's decision

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.980
to spare Negan's life.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.990
Years later, Negan seems by all accounts to
be a changed man, killing Alpha on Carol's

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:37.370
behalf and actively working to prove his loyalty
to Daryl.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:41.460
It seems at this juncture that Negan's years-long
change of heart is real... and he's no longer

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.540
in prison.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:46.680
What will Maggie do when she finds this brutal
ex-ruler, the man who killed Glenn, is freely

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.080
out and about?

